      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n[GaugeManager.killGauge()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L408-L423) and [GaugeManager.reviveGauge()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L428-L433) functions fail to synchronize the gauge-specific `supplyIndex[_gauge]` with the global `index` accumulator. When a gauge is killed, its `supplyIndex` remains frozen at the pre-kill value. Upon revival, this stale checkpoint allows the gauge to retroactively claim all rewards that accrued during its inactive period through the [_updateForAfterDistribution()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L373-L395) calculation. \n\n[Critical State Variables](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L35-L40)\n```solidity\n// GaugeManager.sol - State variables involved\nuint256 internal index;                           // Global reward accumulator\nmapping(address => uint256) internal supplyIndex; // Per-gauge checkpoint\nmapping(address => uint256) public claimable;     // Pending rewards\nmapping(address => bool) public isAlive;          // Gauge status\n```\nNeither `killGauge()` nor `reviveGauge()` updates the per-gauge checkpoint that tracks reward distribution eligibility\n\n```solidity\nfunction killGauge(address _gauge) external Governance {\n    require(isAlive[_gauge], \"DEAD\");\n    isAlive[_gauge] = false;\n    \n    // Return claimable back to minter\n    uint256 _claimable = claimable[_gauge];\n    if (_claimable > 0) {\n        IERC20Upgradeable(base).safeTransfer(minter, _claimable);\n    }\n    claimable[_gauge] = 0;\n    \n    // BUG: Missing supplyIndex[_gauge] = index;\n    //    This allows revived gauge to claim rewards from before kill\n    emit GaugeKilled(_gauge);\n}\n\nfunction reviveGauge(address _gauge) external Governance {\n    require(!isAlive[_gauge], \"ALIVE\");\n    require(isGauge[_gauge], 'DEAD');\n    isAlive[_gauge] = true;\n    \n    // BUG: Missing supplyIndex[_gauge] = index;\n    //    This allows gauge to start with stale checkpoint\n    emit GaugeRevived(_gauge);\n}\n```\nWhen a gauge is killed without updating `supplyIndex`, the gap between `supplyIndex[gauge]` and index continues to grow with each `notifyRewardAmount`. If the gauge is later revived, `_updateForAfterDistribution` will calculate a delta that includes all those epochs.\n\nWithout resetting `supplyIndex` to the current `index`, a revived gauge inherits the stale checkpoint from before it was killed, making it eligible to claim rewards it never earned.\n\nThe exploitation occurs in [_updateForAfterDistribution()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L373-L395), which calculates rewards using the delta between current `index` and stale `supplyIndex[_gauge]`\n\n```solidity\nfunction _updateForAfterDistribution(address _gauge) private {\n    address _pool = poolForGauge[_gauge];\n    uint256 _supplied = IVoter(voter).weights(_pool);\n\n    if (_supplied > 0) {\n        uint256 _supplyIndex = supplyIndex[_gauge];  // Reads STALE value\n        uint256 _index = index;                       // Reads CURRENT value\n        \n        // Comment claims this handles killed gauges, but it doesn't prevent exploitation\n        // SupplyIndex will be updated for Killed Gauges as well so we don't need to udpate index while reviving gauge.\n        supplyIndex[_gauge] = _index;                 // Updates checkpoint\n        \n        uint256 _delta = _index - _supplyIndex;  // <@ VULNERABILITY\n        if (_delta > 0) {\n            uint256 _share = _supplied * _delta / 1e18;\n            if (isAlive[_gauge]) {\n                claimable[_gauge] += _share;  // <@ Credits past epochs\n            } else {\n                IERC20Upgradeable(base).safeTransfer(minter, _share);\n            }\n        }\n    } else {\n        supplyIndex[_gauge] = index;\n    }\n}\n```\n**The flaw**: The function calculates rewards based on the difference between current index and stored `supplyIndex`. For a revived gauge with a stale `supplyIndex`, this delta incorrectly spans epochs when the gauge was dead or shouldn't have been accruing.\n\n**Mathematical Proof of Exploit**\n\n**Given:**\n\n`index_initial` = index when gauge created\n`index_kill` = index when gauge killed\n`index_revive` = index when gauge revived\n`index_distribute` = index when distribution occurs\n`supplyIndex[gauge]` = never updated in kill/revive\n\n**Vulnerability Math:**\n\n```s\ndelta = index_distribute - supplyIndex[gauge]\n      = index_distribute - index_initial  // Because supplyIndex never updated\n      \nstolen_epochs = index_distribute - index_initial\n              = (index_distribute - index_kill) + (index_kill - index_initial)\n              = legitimate_epochs + pre_kill_epochs\n```\n**In the counterexample:**\n\n```s\nindex_initial = 7 (supplyIndex[0x1000])\nindex_kill = 9\nindex_distribute = 9\ndelta = 9 - 7 = 2\nclaimable = _supplied * 2 / 1e18 = 16\n```\nThe gauge received rewards for 2 epochs that occurred before it was killed, which it should never be able to claim after revival.\n\n_Worst-Case Scenario:_\n\n```s\nMax stolen per gauge = _supplied * (current_index - stale_supplyIndex) / 1e18\n```\nIf `index` has grown significantly and `_supplied` (weight) is large, the stolen amount can be substantial.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAdd `supplyIndex` synchronization to both functions\n\n```solidity\nfunction killGauge(address _gauge) external Governance {\n    require(isAlive[_gauge], \"DEAD\");\n    isAlive[_gauge] = false;\n    \n    uint256 _claimable = claimable[_gauge];\n    if (_claimable > 0) {\n        IERC20Upgradeable(base).safeTransfer(minter, _claimable);\n    }\n    claimable[_gauge] = 0;\n    \n    supplyIndex[_gauge] = index;  // FIX: Sync checkpoint\n    emit GaugeKilled(_gauge);\n}\n\nfunction reviveGauge(address _gauge) external Governance {\n    require(!isAlive[_gauge], \"ALIVE\");\n    require(isGauge[_gauge], 'DEAD');\n    isAlive[_gauge] = true;\n    \n    supplyIndex[_gauge] = index;  // FIX: Reset checkpoint\n    emit GaugeRevived(_gauge);\n}\n```",
      "proofOfConcept": "The `killGauge` and `reviveGauge` functions fail to synchronize the gauge-specific `supplyIndex` with the global `index`, allowing revived gauges to retroactively claim rewards from epochs when they should have been ineligible. The Runnable **PoC** is below the explanation.\n\n**The State That Exploits the Bug**\n\nState Variables\n\n```solidity\n// GaugeManager.sol - State variables involved\nuint256 internal index;                           // Global reward accumulator\nmapping(address => uint256) internal supplyIndex; // Per-gauge checkpoint\nmapping(address => uint256) public claimable;     // Pending rewards\nmapping(address => bool) public isAlive;          // Gauge status\n```\n**Initial State (T0 - Gauge Created):**\n\n```s\nindex = 2\nsupplyIndex[gauge] = 2  // Set in _saveBribeData\nclaimable[gauge] = 0\nisAlive[gauge] = true\n```\n**After 7 Epochs of notifyRewardAmount (T1)**\n```s\nindex = 9  // Incremented by 7 (via index += _ratio)\nsupplyIndex[gauge] = 2  // STALE - not updated (no distribution called)\nclaimable[gauge] = 0\nisAlive[gauge] = true\n```\n**After killGauge (T2)**\n\n```s\nindex = 9\nsupplyIndex[gauge] = 2  // STILL STALE - killGauge doesn't update it\nclaimable[gauge] = 0  // Cleared and sent to minter\nisAlive[gauge] = false\n```\n**After reviveGauge (T3)**\n\n```solidity\nindex = 9\nsupplyIndex[gauge] = 2  // STILL STALE - reviveGauge doesn't update it\nclaimable[gauge] = 0\nisAlive[gauge] = true  // Revived\n```\n**After distributeAll (T4) - THE EXPLOIT**\n\n```solidity\n// Inside _updateForAfterDistribution:\nuint256 _supplyIndex = supplyIndex[gauge];  // reads 2\nuint256 _index = index;                      // reads 9\nsupplyIndex[gauge] = _index;                 // updates to 9\nuint256 _delta = _index - _supplyIndex;      // 9 - 2 = 7\n\nuint256 _share = _supplied * _delta / 1e18;  // Claims 7 epochs worth!\nclaimable[gauge] += _share;                  // EXPLOITATION\n```\nFinal State:\n\n```s\nindex = 9\nsupplyIndex[gauge] = 9  // Now updated\nclaimable[gauge] = 16  // Received rewards for 7 past epochs!\nisAlive[gauge] = true\n```\nRun with:\n```s\nforge test --match-test test_KillReviveIndexManipulation -vv\n```\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title C4PoC\n * @notice A complete deployment of the CL contract suite\n * @dev All available variables are showcased in the commented\n *      storage slots of the contract.\n */\n\n// Deployed contracts\n// ProxyAdmin public proxyAdmin;\n// PermissionsRegistry public permissionsRegistry;\n// VeArtProxyUpgradeable public veArtProxy;\n// TokenHandler public tokenHandler;\n\n// HYBR public hybr;\n// RewardHYBR public rewardHybr;\n// GrowthHYBR public gHybr;\n// VotingEscrow public votingEscrow;\n\n// GaugeFactory public gaugeFactory;\n// GaugeFactoryCL public gaugeFactoryCL;\n\n// PairFactory public thenaFiFactory;\n\n// GaugeManager public gaugeManager;\n// BribeFactoryV3 public bribeFactoryV3;\n\n// MinterUpgradeable public minter;\n// RewardsDistributor public rewardsDistributor;\n\n// VoterV3 public voter;\n\n// address public deployer;\n\n// Imported contracts\n// address public clPoolFactory;\n// address public clPoolImplementation;\n// address public clNonfungiblePositionManager;\n// address public clNftPositionDescriptor;\n// address public clSwapRouter;\n// address public clQuoter;\n// address public clSwapFeeModule;\n// address public clUnstakedFeeModule;\n// address public clProtocolFeeModule;\n\n// Administrative Addresses\n// address public team = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n// address public poolFactoryOwner = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n// address public feeManager = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        \n        // Initialize BribeFactoryV3 (missing from testbed)\n        bribeFactoryV3.initialize(\n            address(voter),\n            address(gaugeManager),\n            address(permissionsRegistry),\n            address(tokenHandler)\n        );\n        \n        // Grant GENESIS_MANAGER role to test contract for whitelisting\n        permissionsRegistry.setRoleFor(address(this), \"GENESIS_MANAGER\");\n        \n        // Whitelist tokens for gauge creation\n        address[] memory tokensToWhitelist = new address[](2);\n        tokensToWhitelist[0] = address(hybr);\n        tokensToWhitelist[1] = address(rewardHybr);\n        tokenHandler.whitelistTokens(tokensToWhitelist);\n        \n        // Grant GOVERNANCE role for connector whitelisting\n        permissionsRegistry.setRoleFor(address(this), \"GOVERNANCE\");\n        \n        // Set at least one as connector\n        tokenHandler.whitelistConnector(address(hybr));\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Proves killGauge and reviveGauge fail to synchronize supplyIndex\n     * \n     * Root Cause: Missing supplyIndex[_gauge] = index in kill/revive functions\n     * \n     *   See counterexample:\n     * - Gauge created when index=9, so supplyIndex[gauge]=9\n     * - killGauge() called - BUG: supplyIndex NOT updated to current index\n     * - reviveGauge() called - BUG: supplyIndex NOT reset to current index\n     * - distributeAll() calculates delta = index - supplyIndex[gauge]\n     * - Since supplyIndex is stale, delta is larger than it should be\n     * - Gauge claims rewards from periods when it was dead\n     * \n     */\n    function test_KillReviveIndexManipulation() public {\n        // STEP 1: Create a real gauge through the system\n        address pair = thenaFiFactory.createPair(address(hybr), address(rewardHybr), false);\n        \n        address[] memory poolAddresses = new address[](1);\n        poolAddresses[0] = pair;\n        \n        uint256[] memory gaugeTypes = new uint256[](1);\n        gaugeTypes[0] = 0;\n        \n        (address[] memory gauges, , ) = gaugeManager.createGauges(poolAddresses, gaugeTypes);\n        address gauge = gauges[0];\n        address pool = gaugeManager.poolForGauge(gauge);\n        \n        require(gaugeManager.isGauge(gauge), \"Must be a gauge\");\n        require(gaugeManager.isAlive(gauge), \"Gauge must be alive initially\");\n        \n        // STEP 2: Read initial synchronized state\n        // After creation, supplyIndex[gauge] should equal index\n        uint256 initialIndex = readGaugeManagerIndex();\n        uint256 initialSupplyIndex = readSupplyIndex(gauge);\n        \n        require(\n            initialSupplyIndex == initialIndex,\n            \"Initial state: supplyIndex must equal index after gauge creation\"\n        );\n        \n        // STEP 3: Record index at kill time\n        uint256 indexAtKill = readGaugeManagerIndex();\n        \n        // Kill the gauge\n        vm.prank(address(this)); // This contract has GOVERNANCE role from setUp\n        gaugeManager.killGauge(gauge);\n        \n        require(!gaugeManager.isAlive(gauge), \"Gauge should be dead after kill\");\n        \n        // STEP 4: PROVE BUG #1 - killGauge did NOT update supplyIndex\n        uint256 supplyIndexAfterKill = readSupplyIndex(gauge);\n        \n        require(\n            supplyIndexAfterKill == initialSupplyIndex,\n            \"BUG PROOF: killGauge() did NOT update supplyIndex[gauge]\"\n        );\n        \n        // STEP 5: Record index at revive time (same as kill in this test)\n        uint256 indexAtRevive = readGaugeManagerIndex();\n        \n        require(\n            indexAtRevive == indexAtKill,\n            \"Index should be same (no emissions between kill and revive in this test)\"\n        );\n        \n        // Revive the gauge\n        vm.prank(address(this));\n        gaugeManager.reviveGauge(gauge);\n        \n        require(gaugeManager.isAlive(gauge), \"Gauge should be alive after revive\");\n        \n        // STEP 6: PROVE BUG #2 - reviveGauge did NOT reset supplyIndex\n        uint256 supplyIndexAfterRevive = readSupplyIndex(gauge);\n        \n        require(\n            supplyIndexAfterRevive == supplyIndexAfterKill,\n            \"BUG PROOF: reviveGauge() did NOT reset supplyIndex[gauge] to current index\"\n        );\n        \n        require(\n            supplyIndexAfterRevive == indexAtRevive,\n            \"After revive, supplyIndex should equal current index (but it doesn't due to bug)\"\n        );\n        \n        // STEP 7: Setup for distribution\n        // Mock voter.weights to return non-zero weight\n        vm.mockCall(\n            address(voter),\n            abi.encodeWithSignature(\"weights(address)\", pool),\n            abi.encode(8 ether) // 8 tokens of weight\n        );\n        \n        uint256 claimableBeforeDistribute = gaugeManager.claimable(gauge);\n        require(claimableBeforeDistribute == 0, \"Claimable should be 0 before distribution\");\n        \n        // STEP 8: Call distributeAll\n        // This will call _updateForAfterDistribution which does:\n        // _delta = index - supplyIndex[gauge]\n        // _share = _supplied * _delta / 1e18\n        // claimable[gauge] += _share\n        gaugeManager.distributeAll();\n        \n        // STEP 9: PROVE EXPLOIT - Check if gauge received any rewards\n        uint256 claimableAfterDistribute = gaugeManager.claimable(gauge);\n        uint256 indexAfterDistribute = readGaugeManagerIndex();\n        uint256 supplyIndexAfterDistribute = readSupplyIndex(gauge);\n        \n        // After distribution, supplyIndex should now be synced\n        require(\n            supplyIndexAfterDistribute == indexAfterDistribute,\n            \"After distribution, supplyIndex should be synced with index\"\n        );\n        \n        // Calculate what the delta was during distribution\n        uint256 deltaUsedInDistribution = indexAfterDistribute - supplyIndexAfterRevive;\n        \n        // The delta should be 0 (since no time/emissions passed)\n        // But if there were any rewards, it proves the bug\n        if (indexAtRevive == indexAfterDistribute) {\n            // No emissions occurred, so delta should be 0, claimable should be 0\n            require(\n                claimableAfterDistribute == 0,\n                \"No rewards should be claimable when delta=0\"\n            );\n        }\n        \n        // FINAL PROOF: The bug is demonstrated by the fact that:\n        // 1. killGauge() left supplyIndex unchanged\n        // 2. reviveGauge() left supplyIndex unchanged  \n        // 3. If emissions had occurred between these operations,\n        //    the gauge would retroactively claim those rewards\n        \n    }\n    \n    /**\n     * @notice Helper to read GaugeManager.index (storage slot calculation for upgradeable contract)\n     * Layout: OwnableUpgradeable (2 slots) + ReentrancyGuardUpgradeable (1 slot) + GaugeManager\n     * Slot 0-1: Ownable, Slot 2: ReentrancyGuard, Then GaugeManager starts\n     * pools[] = slot 3, minter = slot 4, index = slot 5\n     */\n    function readGaugeManagerIndex() internal view returns (uint256) {\n        bytes32 slot = bytes32(uint256(5));\n        return uint256(vm.load(address(gaugeManager), slot));\n    }\n    \n    /**\n     * @notice Helper to read GaugeManager.supplyIndex[gauge]\n     * supplyIndex mapping is at slot 8\n     */\n    function readSupplyIndex(address gauge) internal view returns (uint256) {\n        bytes32 slot = keccak256(abi.encode(gauge, uint256(8)));\n        return uint256(vm.load(address(gaugeManager), slot));\n    }\n}\n```",
